  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer of resistance $100 \\Omega$ when connected in series with $400 \\Omega$ measures a voltage of upto $10 \\mathrm{~V}$. The value of resistance required to convert the galvanometer into ammeter to read upto $10 \\mathrm{~A}$ is $x \\times 10^{-2} \\Omega$. The value of $x$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "34ceK",
      "text": "$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "II07C",
      "text": "$800$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "v1SCP",
      "text": "$20$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "IBpCE",
      "text": "$200$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{i}_{\\mathrm{g}}=\\frac{10}{400+100}=20 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~A}$\nFor ammeter\nLet shunt resistance $=\\mathrm{S}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{i}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{R}=\\left(\\mathrm{i}-\\mathrm{i}_{\\mathrm{g}}\\right) \\mathrm{S} \\\\\n& 20 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 100=10 \\mathrm{~S} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~S}=20 \\times 10^{-2} \\Omega\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
